{
  "title": "25: Al-Furqaan الفرقان",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nتَبٰرَكَ الَّذِىْ نَزَّلَ الْفُرْقَانَ عَلٰى عَبْدِهٖ لِيَكُوْنَ لِلْعٰلَمِيْنَ نَذِيْرَا ۙ‏(1)\nTABAARAKAS-MO LAZEE NAZZALAL AL-FURQAANA A’LAA A’ABDEH LEYAKOONA LIL-A’AALAMEENA NAZEERAA.\nBlessed is He who sent down the criterion to His servant, that it may be an admonition to all creatures;- \nاۨلَّذِىْ لَهٗ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَلَمْ يَتَّخِذْ وَلَدًا وَّلَمْ يَكُنْ لَّهٗ شَرِيْكٌ فِى الْمُلْكِ وَخَلَقَ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ فَقَدَّرَهٗ تَقْدِيْرًا‏(2)\nLAZEE LAHU MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA LAM YATTAKHEZ LAAHO LAM YAKUL LAHU SHAREEKUN FIL AL-MULKE WA KHALAQAL KULLA SHAY-IN FAQADDARAHU TAQDEERAA.\nHe to whom belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth: no son has He begotten, nor has He a partner in His dominion: it is He who created all things, and ordered them in due proportions. \nوَاتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اٰلِهَةً لَّا يَخْلُقُوْنَ شَيْئًا وَّهُمْ يُخْلَقُوْنَ وَلَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ لِاَنْفُسِهِمْ ضَرًّا وَّلَا نَفْعًا وَّلَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ مَوْتًا وَّلَا حَيٰوةً وَّلَا نُشُوْرًا‏(3)\nWAT-TAKHAZOO MIN DOONEHI AALEHATAL LAA YAKHLUQOONA SHAY-ANW WA HUM YUKHLAQOONA WA LAA YAMLEKOONA LE-ANFOSEHIM BEKUM WA LAA BEKUM WA LAA YAMLEKOONA MAWTAN WA LAA HAYWTAN WA LAA NUSHOORAN.\nYet have they taken, besides him, gods that can create nothing but are themselves created; that have no control of hurt or good to themselves; nor can they control death nor life nor resurrection. \nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اِفْكٌ اۨفْتَرٰٮهُ وَاَعَانَهٗ عَلَيْهِ قَوْمٌ اٰخَرُوْنَ‌‌ ۛۚ فَقَدْ جَآءُوْ ظُلْمًا وَّزُوْرًا ۛۚ‏(4)\nWA QAALA LAZEENA KAFAROO IN HAAZAA ILLAA AEFKUN AFTARAAHU WAAA’AANAH A’LAYHE QAWMUN AAAKHAROONA FAQAD JAAA-OO ZULMAWN WWAZOORAN.\nBut the misbelievers say: “Naught is this but a lie which he has forged, and others have helped him at it.” In truth it is they who have put forward an iniquity and a falsehood. \nوَقَالُوْۤا اَسَاطِيْرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ اكْتَتَبَهَا فَهِىَ تُمْلٰى عَلَيْهِ بُكْرَةً وَّاَصِيْلًا‏(5)\nWA QAALOO ASAATEERUL AWWALEEN AKTATABAHAA FAHEYA TUMLAA A’LAYHE BUKRATANW WA ASEELAA.\nAnd they say: “Tales of the ancients, which he has caused to be written: and they are dictated before him morning and evening.” \nقُلْ اَنْزَلَهُ الَّذِىْ يَعْلَمُ السِّرَّ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ غَفُوْرًا رَّحِيْمًا‏(6)\nQUL AANZALAHU LAZEE YA’LAMO AS-SERRA FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ INNAHU KAANA GHAFOORAR RAHEEMAA.\nSay: “The (Qur'an) was sent down by Him who knows the mystery (that is) in the heavens and the earth: verily He is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful.” \nوَقَالُوْا مَالِ هٰذَا الرَّسُوْلِ يَاْكُلُ الطَّعَامَ وَيَمْشِىْ فِى الْاَسْوَاقِ‌ ؕ لَوْلَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْهِ مَلَكٌ فَيَكُوْنَ مَعَهٗ نَذِيْرًا ۙ‏(7)\nWA QAALOO MAALE HAAZAA RASOOLE YAAKULU TA-A’AMA WAYAMSHEAA FIL AL-AASWAAQE LAWLAA UNZELA ELAYHE MALAKUN FA YAKOONA MA-A’HU NAZEERAN.\nAnd they say: “What sort of a messenger is this, who eats food, and walks through the streets? Why has not an angel been sent down to him to give admonition with him? \nاَوْ يُلْقٰٓى اِلَيْهِ كَنْزٌ اَوْ تَكُوْنُ لَهٗ جَنَّةٌ يَّاْكُلُ مِنْهَا‌ ؕ وَقَالَ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ اِنْ تَتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا رَجُلًا مَّسْحُوْرًا‏(8)\nAW YULQAAA ELAYHE KANZUN AW TAKOONO LAHU JANNATUM YYAAKULU MINHAA WA QAALA ZAALEMOON IN TATTABEU’OONA ILLAA RAJULAN MMASHOORAN.\n“Or (Why) has not a treasure been bestowed on him, or why has he (not) a garden for enjoyment?” The wicked say: “Ye follow none other than a man bewitched.” \nاُنْظُرْ كَيْفَ ضَرَبُوْا لَكَ الْاَمْثَالَ فَضَلُّوْا فَلَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ سَبِيْلاً‏(9)\nAUNZUR KAYFA ZARABOOA LAKA AL-AAMSAALA FAZALLOOA FALAA YASTATEE-O’ONA SABEELAAN.\nSee what kinds of comparisons they make for thee! But they have gone astray, and never a way will they be able to find! \nتَبٰرَكَ الَّذِىْۤ اِنْ شَآءَ جَعَلَ لَكَ خَيْرًا مِّنْ ذٰ لِكَ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ ۙ وَيَجْعَلْ لَّكَ قُصُوْرًا‏(10)\nTABAARAKAS-MO LAZEE IN SHAAA-AL JA-A’LA LAKA KHAYRAN MIN ZAA LEKA JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO WA YAJ-A’L LAKA QUSOORAN.\nBlessed is He who, if that were His will, could give thee better (things) than those, Gardens beneath which rivers flow; and He could give thee palaces (secure to dwell in). \nبَلْ كَذَّبُوْا بِالسَّاعَةِ‌ وَاَعْتَدْنَا لِمَنْ كَذَّبَ بِالسَّاعَةِ سَعِيْرًا‌ ۚ‏(11)\nBAL KAZZABOO BEALSSAAA’ATE WA A-ATADNAA LEMAN-Y KAZZABA BEALSSAAA’ATE SA-E’ERAA.\nNay they deny the hour (of the judgment to come): but We have prepared a blazing fire for such as deny the hour: \nاِذَا رَاَتْهُمْ مِّنْ مَّكَانٍۢ بَعِيْدٍ سَمِعُوْا لَهَا تَغَيُّظًا وَّزَفِيْرًا‏(12)\nEZAA RAATHUM MIN MAKAANIM BA-E’ED SAMEO’O LAHAA TAGHAYZAN WWAZAFEERAN.\nWhen it sees them from a place fAr off, they will hear its fury and its ranging sigh. \nوَاِذَاۤ اُلْقُوْا مِنْهَا مَكَانًا ضَيِّقًا مُّقَرَّنِيْنَ دَعَوْا هُنَالِكَ ثُبُوْرًا ؕ‏(13)\nWA EZAA ULQOO MINHAA MAKAANAN ZAYQAN MMUQARRANEENA DA-A’W HONAALEKAB SOBOORANW.\nAnd when they are cast, bound together into a constricted place therein, they will pLead for destruction there and then! \nلَا تَدْعُوا الْيَوْمَ ثُبُوْرًا وَّاحِدًا وَّادْعُوْا ثُبُوْرًا كَثِيْرًا‏(14)\nLAA TADU’OOA YAWMA SOBOORANW WAAHEDANW WWAADU’OOA SOBOORANW KASEERAA.\n“This day plead not for a single destruction: plead for destruction oft-repeated!” \nقُلْ اَذٰ لِكَ خَيْرٌ اَمْ جَنَّةُ الْخُلْدِ الَّتِىْ وُعِدَ الْمُتَّقُوْنَ ‌ؕ كَانَتْ لَهُمْ جَزَآءً وَّمَصِيْرًا‏(15)\nQUL AAZAA LEKA KHAYRUL AM JANNATU AL-KHULDE LATEE WUE’EDA MUTTAQOON KAANAT LAHUM JA-ZAAA-AWN WWAMASEERAN.\nSay: “Is that best, or the eternal garden, promised to the righteous? for them, that is a reward as well as a goal (of attainment). \nلَّهُمْ فِيْهَا مَا يَشَآءُوْنَ خٰلِدِيْنَ‌ ؕ كَانَ عَلٰى رَبِّكَ وَعْدًا مَّسْئُوْلًا‏(16)\nLAHUM FEEHAA MAA YASHAAOONA KHAALEDEENA KAANA A’LAA RABBEKA WA’DAN MMASOOLAN.\n“For them there will be therein all that they wish for: they will dwell (there) for aye: A promise to be prayed for from thy Lord.” \nوَيَوْمَ يَحْشُرُهُمْ وَمَا يَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ فَيَقُوْلُ ءَاَنْتُمْ اَضْلَلْتُمْ عِبَادِىْ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ اَمْ هُمْ ضَلُّوا السَّبِيْلَ ؕ‏(17)\nWA YAWMA YAHSHURUHUM WA MAA YA’BODOON MIN DOONIL LAAHE FAYAQOOLO A-ANTUM AAZLALTUM E’BAADEE HAAOOLAAA-E AM HUM ZALLOOA SABEELA.\nThe day He will gather them together as well as those whom they worship besides Allah, He will ask: “Was it ye who let these My servants astray, or did they stray from the Path themselves?” \nقَالُوْا سُبْحٰنَكَ مَا كَانَ يَنْۢبَغِىْ لَنَاۤ اَنْ نَّتَّخِذَ مِنْ دُوْنِكَ مِنْ اَوْلِيَآءَ وَ لٰكِنْ مَّتَّعْتَهُمْ وَاٰبَآءَهُمْ حَتّٰى نَسُوا الذِّكْرَ‌ۚ وَكَانُوْا قَوْمًۢا بُوْرًا‏(18)\nQAALOO SUBHAANAKA MAA KAANA LAHAA LANAA AN NNATTAKHEZA MIN DOONEKA MIN AAWLEEAAAA WA LAAKEN MMATTAA’TAHUM WA AA-BAAA-AHUM HATTAA NASUL KHASEYAR WA KAANOO QAWMAN BOORAA.\nThey will say: “Glory to Thee! not meet was it for us that we should take for protectors others besides Thee: But Thou didst bestow, on them and their fathers, good things (in life), until they forgot the Message: for they were a people (worthless and) lost.” \nفَقَدْ كَذَّبُوْكُمْ بِمَا تَقُوْلُوْنَۙ فَمَا تَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ صَرْفًا وَّلَا نَصْرًا‌ۚ وَمَنْ يَّظْلِمْ مِّنْكُمْ نُذِقْهُ عَذَابًا كَبِيْرًا‏(19)\nFAQAD KAZZABOOKUM BEMAA TAQOOLOONA FAMAA TASTATEEU’OONA SARFAN WA LAA NASRAN WA MAN YYAZLEM MINKUM NUZEQHU A’ZAABAN KABEERAA.\n(Allah will say): “Now have they proved you liars in what ye say: so ye cannot avert (your penalty) nor (get) help.” And whoever among you does wrong, him shall We cause to taste of a grievous Penalty. \nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا قَبْلَكَ مِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ اِلَّاۤ اِنَّهُمْ لَيَاْكُلُوْنَ الطَّعَامَ وَيَمْشُوْنَ فِى الْاَسْوَاقِ‌ ؕ وَجَعَلْنَا بَعْضَكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ فِتْنَةً  ؕ اَتَصْبِرُوْنَ‌ۚ وَكَانَ رَبُّكَ بَصِيْرًا‏(20)\nWA MAA ARSALNAA QABLAKA MENAL MURSALEEN ILLAA INNAHUM LAYAAKULOONA TA-A’AMA WAYAMSHOONA FIL AL-AASWAAQE WA JA-A’LNAA BAA’ZAKUM LE-BA’ZIN FETNATAN AATASBEROONA KAANAL RABBOKA BASEERAA.\nAnd the messengers whom We sent before thee were all (men) who ate food and walked through the streets: We have made some of you as a trial for others: will ye have patience? for Allah is One Who sees (all things). \nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَرْجُوْنَ لِقَآءَنَا لَوْلَاۤ اُنْزِلَ عَلَيْنَا الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ اَوْ نَرٰى رَبَّنَا ؕ لَقَدِ اسْتَكْبَرُوْا فِىْۤ اَنْفُسِهِمْ وَعَتَوْ عُتُوًّا كَبِيْرًا‏(21)\nWA QAALA LAZEENA LAA YARJOON LEQAAANAA LAWLAA UNZELA A’LAYNAA TAHMELOHUL AW NARAA RABBANAA LAQADE ASTAKBAROOA FEE ANFOSEHIM WAA’ATAW U’UTOOA KABEERAA.\nSuch as fear not the meeting with Us (for Judgment) say: “Why are not the angels sent down to us, or (why) do we not see our Lord?” Indeed they have an arrogant conceit of themselves, and mighty is the insolence of their impiety! \nيَوْمَ يَرَوْنَ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةَ لَا بُشْرٰى يَوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُجْرِمِيْنَ وَ يَقُوْلُوْنَ حِجْرًا مَّحْجُوْرًا‏(22)\nYAWMA YARAWNAL AL-MALAAAEKATA LAA BUSHRAA YAWMA-EZIN LILMUJREMEEN WA YAQOOLOONA HEJRAN MMAHJOORAN.\nThe Day they see the angels, no joy will there be to the sinners that Day: The (angels) will say: “There is a barrier forbidden (to you) altogether!” \nوَقَدِمْنَاۤ اِلٰى مَا عَمِلُوْا مِنْ عَمَلٍ فَجَعَلْنٰهُ هَبَآءً مَّنْثُوْرًا‏(23)\nWAQADEMNAA ELAA MAA A’MELOO MIN A’AMALIN FA-JA-A’LNAAHO HABAAA-AM MANSOORAA.\nAnd We shall turn to whatever deeds they did (in this life), and We shall make such deeds as floating dust scattered about. \nاَصْحٰبُ الْجَنَّةِ يَوْمَئِذٍ خَيْرٌ مُّسْتَقَرًّا وَّاَحْسَنُ مَقِيْلًا‏(24)\nASHAABUN JANNAH YAWMA-EZIN KHAYRUL MMUSTAQARRAN WWAAHSANU MAQEELAN.\nThe Companions of the Garden will be well, that Day, in their abode, and have the fairest of places for repose. \nوَيَوْمَ تَشَقَّقُ السَّمَآءُ بِالْغَمَامِ وَنُزِّلَ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ تَنْزِيْلًا‏(25)\nWA YAWMA TASHAQQAQU SAMAAA-O BE-GHAMAAME WANUZZELA TAHMELOHUL TANZEELAA.\nThe Day the heaven shall be rent asunder with clouds, and angels shall be sent down, descending (in ranks), \nاَلْمُلْكُ يَوْمَئِذِ اۨلْحَقُّ لِلرَّحْمٰنِ‌ؕ وَكَانَ يَوْمًا عَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ عَسِيْرًا‏(26)\nAALMULKU YAWMAEZE HAQQO LELRRAHMAANE KAANAL YAWMAN A’LAL KAAFEREEN A’ASEERAN.\nThat Day, the dominion as of right and truth, shall be (wholly) for (Allah) Most Merciful: it will be a Day of dire difficulty for the Misbelievers. \nوَيَوْمَ يَعَضُّ الظَّالِمُ عَلٰى يَدَيْهِ يَقُوْلُ يٰلَيْتَنِى اتَّخَذْتُ مَعَ الرَّسُوْلِ سَبِيْلًا‏(27)\nWA YAWMA YAA’AZZU AZ-ZAALEMU A’LAA YADAYHE YAQOOLO YAALAYTANEAA ATTAKHAZTU LAAHA RASOOLE SABEELAA.\nThe Day that the wrong-doer will bite at his hands, he will say, “Oh! would that I had taken a (straight) path with the Messenger! \nيٰوَيْلَتٰى لَيْتَنِىْ لَمْ اَتَّخِذْ فُلَانًا خَلِيْلًا‏(28)\nYAAWAYLATAA LAYTANEAA LAM AATTAKHEZ FULAANAN KHALEELAN.\n“Ah! woe is me! Would that I had never taken such a one for a friend! \nلَقَدْ اَضَلَّنِىْ عَنِ الذِّكْرِ بَعْدَ اِذْ جَآءَنِىْ‌ ؕ وَكَانَ الشَّيْطٰنُ لِلْاِنْسَانِ خَذُوْلًا‏(29)\nLAQAD AAZALLANEAA A’NIL AZ-ZEKRE BA’DA IZ JAAANEAA KAANAL SHAYTAANO INSAANIK KHAZOOLAN.\n“He did lead me astray from the Message (of Allah) after it had come to me! Ah! the Evil One is but a traitor to man!” \nوَقَالَ الرَّسُوْلُ يٰرَبِّ اِنَّ قَوْمِى اتَّخَذُوْا هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنَ مَهْجُوْرًا‏(30)\nWA QAALA RASOOLO YAA RABBE INNAL QAWMEAA ATTAKHAZOOA HAAZAA QURAANA MAHJOORAN.\nThen the Messenger will say: “O my Lord! Truly my people took this Qur'an for just foolish nonsense.” \nوَكَذٰلِكَ جَعَلْنَا لِكُلِّ نَبِىٍّ عَدُوًّا مِّنَ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‌ؕ وَكَفٰى بِرَبِّكَ هَادِيًا وَّنَصِيْرًا‏(31)\nWA KAZAALEKA JA-A’LNAA LEKULLIM NABEAAAIN A’DUWWAL MENAL AL-MUJREMEENA KAFAA BERABBEKA HAADEEA WWANASEERAN.\nThus have We made for every prophet an enemy among the sinners: but enough is thy Lord to guide and to help. \nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَوْلَا نُزِّلَ عَلَيْهِ الْقُرْاٰنُ جُمْلَةً وَّاحِدَةً‌  ‌ۛۚ كَذٰلِكَ ‌ۛۚ لِنُثَبِّتَ بِهٖ فُؤَادَكَ‌ وَرَتَّلْنٰهُ تَرْتِيْلًا‏(32)\nWA QAALA LAZEENA KAFAROO LAWLAA NUZZELA A’LAYHE QUR-AANO JUMLATAN WAAHEDATAN KAZAALEKA LENUSABBETA BEHI FUAADAKA WARATTALNAAHU QUR-AANA.\nThose who reject Faith say: “Why is not the Qur'an revealed to him all at once? Thus (is it revealed), that We may strengthen thy heart thereby, and We have rehearsed it to thee in slow, well-arranged stages, gradually. \nوَلَا يَاْتُوْنَكَ بِمَثَلٍ اِلَّا جِئْنٰكَ بِالْحَقِّ وَاَحْسَنَ تَفْسِيْرًا ؕ‏(33)\nWA LAA YAATOONAKA BEMASALIN ILLAA JENAAKA BIL-HAQQE WA AHSANAL TAFSEERAN.\nAnd no question do they bring to thee but We reveal to thee the truth and the best explanation (thereof). \nاَلَّذِيْنَ يُحْشَرُوْنَ عَلٰى وُجُوْهِهِمْ اِلٰى جَهَنَّمَۙ اُولٰٓئِكَ شَرٌّ مَّكَانًا وَّاَضَلُّ سَبِيْلًا‏(34)\nLAZEENA YUHSHAROONA A’LAA SEEMAAHUM ELAA JAHANNAMA OOLAAA-EKA HOWA MMAKAANAN WWAAZALLU SABEELAA.\nThose who will be gathered to Hell (prone) on their faces, they will be in an evil plight, and, as to Path, most astray. \nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ وَجَعَلْنَا مَعَهٗۤ اَخَاهُ هٰرُوْنَ وَزِيْرًا‌ ۖ‌ ۚ‏(35)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAL KETAABA WA JA-A’LNAA MA-A’HU AAKHAAHU AALO WAZEERAN.\n(Before this,) We sent Moses The Book, and appointed his brother Aaron with him as minister; \nفَقُلْنَا اذْهَبَاۤ اِلَى الْقَوْمِ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَاؕ فَدَمَّرْنٰهُمْ تَدْمِيْرًاؕ‏(36)\nFAQULNAA AZHABAA ELAL QAWMIL LAZEENA KAZZABOO BEAAAYAATENAA FA DAMMARNAAHUM TADMEERAN.\nAnd We command: “Go ye both, to the people who have rejected our Signs:” And those (people) We destroyed with utter destruction. \nوَقَوْمَ نُوْحٍ لَّمَّا كَذَّبُوا الرُّسُلَ اَغْرَقْنٰهُمْ وَجَعَلْنٰهُمْ لِلنَّاسِ اٰيَةً ‌ ؕ وَاَعْتَدْنَا لِلظّٰلِمِيْنَ عَذَابًا اَ لِيْمًا ‌ۖ‌ ۚ‏(37)\nWA QAWMA NOOHIN LAMMAA KAZZABOOA AR-RUSULA AAGHRAQNAAHUM WA JA-A’LNAAHUM LIN-NAASE AAYATAL WA A-ATADNAA LIZ-ZAALEMEENA A’ZAABAN A’ZAABAN ALEEMAA.\nAnd the people of Noah, when they rejected the messengers, We drowned them, and We made them as a Sign for mankind; and We have prepared for (all) wrong-doers a grievous Penalty;- \nوَّعَادًا وَّثَمُوْدَا۟ وَ اَصْحٰبَ الرَّسِّ وَقُرُوْنًۢا بَيْنَ ذٰ لِكَ كَثِيْرًا‏(38)\nWWAA’AADAN WA SAMOODAA WA MASALAN AR-RASSE WA QOROONAN BAYNA ZAA LEKA KASEERAA.\nAs also 'Ad and Thamud, and the Companions of the Rass, and many a generation between them. \nوَكُلًّا ضَرَبْنَا لَهُ الْاَمْثَالَ‌ وَكُلًّا تَبَّرْنَا تَتْبِيْرًا‏(39)\nWAKULLAN ZARABNAA LAHUL AL-AAMSAALA WAKULLAN TABBARNAA TATBEERAN.\nTo each one We set forth Parables and examples; and each one We broke to utter annihilation (for their sins). \nوَلَقَدْ اَتَوْا عَلَى الْقَرْيَةِ الَّتِىْۤ اُمْطِرَتْ مَطَرَ السَّوْءِ‌ ؕ اَفَلَمْ يَكُوْنُوْا يَرَوْنَهَا ‌ۚ بَلْ كَانُوْا لَا يَرْجُوْنَ نُشُوْرًا‏(40)\nWA LAQAD ATAW A’LAL QARYAH LATEE AUMTERAT MATARA SAW A-FALAM YAKOONOOA YARAWNAHAA BAL KAANOO LAA YARJOON NUSHOORAN.\nAnd the (Unbelievers) must indeed have passed by the town on which was rained a shower of evil: did they not then see it (with their own eyes)? But they fear not the Resurrection. \nوَاِذَا رَاَوْكَ اِنْ يَّتَّخِذُوْنَكَ اِلَّا هُزُوًا ؕ اَهٰذَا الَّذِىْ بَعَثَ اللّٰهُ رَسُوْلًا‏(41)\nWA EZAA RAAWKA IN YYATTAKHEZOONAKA ILLAA HOZOWANW AAHAAZAA LAZEE BA-A’SA LAAHO RASOOLAM.\nWhen they see thee, they treat thee no otherwise than in mockery: “Is this the one whom Allah has sent as a messenger?” \nاِنْ كَادَ لَيُضِلُّنَا عَنْ اٰلِهَتِنَا لَوْ لَاۤ اَنْ صَبَرْنَا عَلَيْهَا‌ ؕ وَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُوْنَ حِيْنَ يَرَوْنَ الْعَذَابَ مَنْ اَضَلُّ سَبِيْلًا‏(42)\nIN KAADA LAYUZELLUNAA A’N AAALEHATENAA LAW LAA AN SABARNAA A’LAYHAA WA SAWFA YA’LAMOON HEENA YARAWNAL A’ZAABA MAN AZALLO SABEELAA.\n“He indeed would well-nigh have misled us from our gods, had it not been that we were constant to them!” - Soon will they know, when they see the Penalty, who it is that is most misled in Path! \nاَرَءَيْتَ مَنِ اتَّخَذَ اِلٰهَهٗ هَوٰٮهُ ؕ اَفَاَنْتَ تَكُوْنُ عَلَيْهِ وَكِيْلًا ۙ‏(43)\nA-RA-AYTA MANIS TAKHAZA AELAAHAH HAWHU AAFAANTA TAKOONO A’LAYHE WAKEELAA.\nSeest thou such a one as taketh for his god his own passion (or impulse)? Couldst thou be a disposer of affairs for him? \nاَمْ تَحْسَبُ اَنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ يَسْمَعُوْنَ اَوْ يَعْقِلُوْنَ‌ ؕ اِنْ هُمْ اِلَّا كَالْاَنْعَامِ‌ بَلْ هُمْ اَضَلُّ سَبِيْلًا‏(44)\nAM TAHSABU ANNAL AKSARAHUM YAS-MA-O’ONA AW YA’QELOON IN HUM ILLAA KAALAANA’AAME BAL HUM AZALLO SABEELAA.\nOr thinkest thou that most of them listen or understand? They are only like cattle;- nay, they are worse astray in Path. \nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ كَيْفَ مَدَّ الظِّلَّ‌ ۚ وَلَوْ شَآءَ لَجَعَلَهٗ سَاكِنًا‌ ۚ ثُمَّ جَعَلْنَا الشَّمْسَ عَلَيْهِ دَلِيْلًا ۙ‏(45)\nALAM TARA ELAA RABBEKA KAYFA MADDA AZ-ZELLA WA LAW SHAAA-AL LAJAA’ALAH SAAKENAN SUMMA JA-A’LNAA SHAMSA A’LAYHE DALEELAN.\nHast thou not turned thy vision to thy Lord? How He doth prolong the shadow! If He willed, He could make it stationary! then do We make the sun its guide; \nثُمَّ قَبَضْنٰهُ اِلَيْنَا قَبْضًا يَّسِيْرًا‏(46)\nSUMMA QABAZNAAHU ELAYNAA QABZAN YASEERANW.\nThen We draw it in towards Ourselves, a contraction by easy stages. \nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الَّيْلَ لِبَاسًا وَّالنَّوْمَ سُبَاتًا وَّجَعَلَ النَّهَارَ نُشُوْرًا‏(47)\nWA HOWA LAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL LAYLA LEBAASANW WWAALNNAWMA SOBAATANW ANHAARAWN NAHAARA NUSHOORAN.\nAnd He it is Who makes the Night as a Robe for you, and Sleep as Repose, and makes the Day (as it were) a Resurrection. \nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَرْسَلَ الرِّيٰحَ بُشْرًۢا بَيْنَ يَدَىْ رَحْمَتِهٖ‌ۚ وَاَنْزَلْنَا مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً طَهُوْرًا ۙ‏(48)\nWA HOWA LAZEE ARSALA REYAAHA BUSHRAM BAYNA YADAY FEE WA ANZALNAA MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN TAHOORAA.\nAnd He it is Who sends the winds as heralds of glad tidings, going before His mercy, and We send down pure water from the sky, \nلِّنُحْیِۦَ بِهٖ بَلْدَةً مَّيْتًا وَّنُسْقِيَهٗ مِمَّا خَلَقْنَاۤ اَنْعَامًا وَّاَنَاسِىَّ كَثِيْرًا‏(49)\nLENUH BEHI BALDATAN MMAYTAN WWANUSQEEH MIMMAA KHALAQNAL AN-A’AMAN WWAANAASEAAAA KASEERAA.\nThat with it We may give life to a dead land, and slake the thirst of things We have created, cattle and men in great numbers. \nوَلَقَدْ صَرَّفْنٰهُ بَيْنَهُمْ لِيَذَّكَّرُوْا ‌ ۖ ا فَاَبٰٓى اَكْثَرُ النَّاسِ اِلَّا كُفُوْرًا‏(50)\nWA LAQAD SARRAFNAAHU BAYNAHUM LEEZZAKKAROOA A FAABAAA AAKSARU NAASE ILLAA KUFOORAN.\nAnd We have distributed the (water) amongst them, in order that they may celebrate (our) praises, but most men are averse (to aught) but (rank) ingratitude. \nوَلَوْ شِئْنَا لَبَعَثْنَا فِىْ كُلِّ قَرْيَةٍ نَّذِيْرًا ‌ۖ ‏(51)\nWA LAW SHE’NAA LABAA’ASNAA FEE KULLE QARYATINW NNAZEERAN.\nHad it been Our Will, We could have sent a warner to every centre of population. \nفَلَا تُطِعِ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ وَ جَاهِدْهُمْ بِهٖ جِهَادًا كَبِيْرًا‏(52)\nFALAA LAA KAAFEREEN WA JAAHEDHUM BEHI JEHAADAN KABEERAA.\nTherefore listen not to the Unbelievers, but strive against them with the utmost strenuousness, with the (Qur'an). \nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ مَرَجَ الْبَحْرَيْنِ هٰذَا عَذْبٌ فُرَاتٌ وَّهٰذَا مِلْحٌ‌ اُجَاجٌ ۚ وَجَعَلَ بَيْنَهُمَا بَرْزَخًا وَّحِجْرًا مَّحْجُوْرًا‏(53)\nWA HOWA LAZEE MARAJAL WA HAAZAA A’AZBUN FURAATUN WWAHAAZAA MELHUN AUJAAJUN WA BAYNAHOMAA BARZAKHAN WWAHEJRAN MMAHJOORAN.\nIt is He Who has let free the two bodies of flowing water: One palatable and sweet, and the other salt and bitter; yet has He made a barrier between them, a partition that is forbidden to be passed. \nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ مِنَ الْمَآءِ بَشَرًا فَجَعَلَهٗ نَسَبًا وَّ صِهْرًا‌ ؕ وَكَانَ رَبُّكَ قَدِيْرًا‏(54)\nWA HOWA LAZEE KHALAQAL MENAL AL-MAAE BASHARAN FA-JA-A’LAHU NASABAN WA SEHRAN KAANAL RABBOKA QADEERAA.\nIt is He Who has created man from water: then has He established relationships of lineage and marriage: for thy Lord has power (over all things). \nوَيَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا يَنْفَعُهُمْ وَلَا يَضُرُّهُمْ‌ؕ وَكَانَ الْكَافِرُ عَلٰى رَبِّهٖ ظَهِيْرًا‏(55)\nWA YA’BODOON MIN DOONIL LAAHE MAA LAA YANFAU’UHUM WA LAA YAZURRUHUM KAANAL AL-KAAFERU A’LAA RABBEHI ZAHEERAL.\nYet do they worship, besides Allah, things that can neither profit them nor harm them: and the Misbeliever is a helper (of Evil), against his own Lord! \nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنٰكَ اِلَّا مُبَشِّرًا وَّنَذِيْرًا‏(56)\nWA MAA ARSALNAAKA ILLAA MUBASSHERAN WA NAZEERANW.\nBut thee We only sent to give glad tidings and admonition. \nقُلْ مَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ اَجْرٍ اِلَّا مَنْ شَآءَ اَنْ يَّتَّخِذَ اِلٰى رَبِّهٖ سَبِيْلًا‏(57)\nQUL MAA AASALUKUM A’LAYHE MIN AAJRIN ILLAA MAN SHAAA-AL AN YYATTAKHEZA ELAA RABBEHI SABEELAA.\nSay: “No reward do I ask of you for it but this: that each one who will may take a (straight) Path to his Lord.” \nوَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى الْحَىِّ الَّذِىْ لَا يَمُوْتُ وَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِهٖ‌ ؕ وَكَفٰى بِهٖ بِذُنُوْبِ عِبَادِهٖ خَبِيْرَ ا‌ ۛۚ ۙ‏(58)\nWA TAWAKKAL A’LAL HAYYE LAZEE LAA YAMOOTO WASABBEH BEHAMDEH KAFAA BEHI BEZUNOOBE E’BAADEHI KHABEERA A.\nAnd put thy trust in Him Who lives and dies not; and celebrate his praise; and enough is He to be acquainted with the faults of His servants;- \nاۨلَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا فِىْ سِتَّةِ اَيَّامٍ ثُمَّ اسْتَوٰى عَلَى الْعَرْشِ ‌ۛۚ اَلرَّحْمٰنُ فَسْئَلْ بِهٖ خَبِيْرًا‏(59)\nLAZEE KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA FEE SETTATE AYYAAMIN SUMMA TAWAA A’LAL A’RSHIL AR-RAHMAAN FASAL BEHI KHABEERAA.\nHe Who created the heavens and the earth and all that is between, in six days, and is firmly established on the Throne (of Authority): Allah Most Gracious: ask thou, then, about Him of any acquainted (with such things). \nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمُ اسْجُدُوْا لِلرَّحْمٰنِ قَالُوْا وَمَا الرَّحْمٰنُ اَنَسْجُدُ لِمَا تَاْمُرُنَا وَزَادَهُمْ نُفُوْرًا ۩‏(60)\nWA EZAA QEELA LAHOMUL JODOO LELRRAHMAANE QAALOO WA MAA RAHMAANO AANASJUDU LEMAKH TAAMURUNAA WA ZAADAHUM NUFOORAN.\nWhen it is said to them, “Prostrate to (Allah) Most Gracious!”, they say, “And what is (Allah) Most Gracious? Shall we prostrate to that which thou commandest us?” And it increases their flight (from the Truth). [۩] \nتَبٰرَكَ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ فِى السَّمَآءِ بُرُوْجًا وَّجَعَلَ فِيْهَا سِرٰجًا وَّقَمَرًا مُّنِيْرًا‏(61)\nTABAARAKAS-MO LAZEE JA-A’LA FIL SAMAAA-E BUROOJAN ANHAARAWN FEEHAA SERAAJAN WWAQAMARAN MONEERAA.\nBlessed is He Who made constellations in the skies, and placed therein a Lamp and a Moon giving light; \nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ الَّيْلَ وَالنَّهَارَ خِلْفَةً لِّمَنْ اَرَادَ اَنْ يَّذَّكَّرَ اَوْ اَرَادَ شُكُوْرًا‏(62)\nWA HOWA LAZEE JA-A’LA LAYLA WAN NAHAARA KHELFATAN LEMAN ARAADA AN YYAZZAKKARA AW ARAADA SHOKOORAA.\nAnd it is He Who made the Night and the Day to follow each other: for such as have the will to celebrate His praises or to show their gratitude. \nوَعِبَادُ الرَّحْمٰنِ الَّذِيْنَ يَمْشُوْنَ عَلَى الْاَرْضِ هَوْنًا وَّاِذَا خَاطَبَهُمُ الْجٰهِلُوْنَ قَالُوْا سَلٰمًا‏(63)\nWAE’EBAADU RAHMAANIR LAZEENA YAMSHOONA A’LAL ARZE HAWNAN WWAAZAA KHAATABAHUMU AL-JAAHELOONA QAALOO SALAAMAA.\nAnd the servants of (Allah) Most Gracious are those who walk on the earth in humility, and when the ignorant address them, they say, “Peace!”; \nوَالَّذِيْنَ يَبِيْتُوْنَ لِرَبِّهِمْ سُجَّدًا وَّقِيَامًا‏(64)\nWAL LAZEENA YABEETOONA LE-RABBEHIM SUJJADANW WWAQEEAMAN.\nThose who spend the night in adoration of their Lord prostrate and standing; \nوَالَّذِيْنَ يَقُوْلُوْنَ رَبَّنَا اصْرِفْ عَنَّا عَذَابَ جَهَنَّمَ ‌ۖ  اِنَّ عَذَابَهَا كَانَ غَرَامًا ‌ۖ ‏(65)\nWAL LAZEENA YAQOOLOONA RABBANAA ASREF WAGH A’ZAABAL JAHANNAMA INNAL A’AZAABAHAA KAANA GHARAAMAN.\nThose who say, “Our Lord! avert from us the Wrath of Hell, for its Wrath is indeed an affliction grievous, \nاِنَّهَا سَآءَتْ مُسْتَقَرًّا وَّمُقَامًا‏(66)\nINNAHAA SAAAT MUSTAQARRAN WWAMUQAAMAN.\n“Evil indeed is it as an abode, and as a place to rest in”; \nوَالَّذِيْنَ اِذَاۤ اَنْفَقُوْا لَمْ يُسْرِفُوْا وَلَمْ يَقْتُرُوْا وَكَانَ بَيْنَ ذٰلِكَ قَوَامًا‏(67)\nWAL LAZEENA EZAA ANFAQOO LAM YUSREFOOA WA LAM YAQTUROOA KAANAL BAYNA ZAALEKA QAWAAMAN.\nThose who, when they spend, are not extravagant and not niggardly, but hold a just (balance) between those (extremes); \nوَالَّذِيْنَ لَا يَدْعُوْنَ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ وَلَا يَقْتُلُوْنَ النَّفْسَ الَّتِىْ حَرَّمَ اللّٰهُ اِلَّا بِالْحَقِّ وَلَا يَزْنُوْنَ‌ ۚ وَمَنْ يَّفْعَلْ ذٰ لِكَ يَلْقَ اَثَامًا ۙ‏(68)\nWAL LAZEENA LAA YAD-O’ONA LAAHA LAAHE ELAAHANW AAKHAR WA LAA YAQTULOONA AN-NAFSA LATEE HARRAMA LAAHO ILLAA BIL-HAQQE WA LAA YAZNOONA WA MAN MAN-Y ZAA LEKA YALQA AASAAMAN.\nThose who invoke not, with Allah, any other god, nor slay such life as Allah has made sacred except for just cause, nor commit fornication; - and any that does this (not only) meets punishment. \nيُضٰعَفْ لَهُ الْعَذَابُ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ وَيَخْلُدْ فِيْهٖ مُهَانًا ۖ ‏(69)\nYUZAAA’AF LAHUL A’ZAABO YAWMA QEYAAMATE WAYAKHLUD FEEH MUHAANAN.\n(But) the Penalty on the Day of Judgment will be doubled to him, and he will dwell therein in ignominy, \nاِلَّا مَنْ تَابَ وَاٰمَنَ وَعَمِلَ عَمَلًاصَالِحًا فَاُولٰٓئِكَ يُبَدِّلُ اللّٰهُ سَيِّاٰتِهِمْ حَسَنٰتٍ‌ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ غَفُوْرًا رَّحِيْمًا‏(70)\nILLAA MAN TAABA WA AAMANA WA A’MELA A’AMALANSAALEHAN FA-OOLAAA-EKA YUBADDELU LAAHO SAYYEAATEHIM HASANAATIN KAANAL LAAHO GHAFOORAR RAHEEMAA.\nUnless he repents, believes, and works righteous deeds, for Allah will change the evil of such persons into good, and Allah is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful, \nوَمَنْ تَابَ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا فَاِنَّهٗ يَتُوْبُ اِلَى اللّٰهِ مَتَابًا‏(71)\nWA MAN TAABA WA A’MELA SAALEHAN FA-INNAHU YATOOBU ELAL LAAHE MATAABAN.\nAnd whoever repents and does good has truly turned to Allah with an (acceptable) conversion;- \nوَالَّذِيْنَ لَا يَشْهَدُوْنَ الزُّوْرَۙ وَ اِذَا مَرُّوْا بِاللَّغْوِ مَرُّوْا كِرَامًا‏(72)\nWAL LAZEENA LAA YASHHADOONA AZ-ZOORA WA EZAA MARROO BIL-LAGHWE MARROO KERAAMAN.\nThose who witness no falsehood, and, if they pass by futility, they pass by it with honourable (avoidance); \nوَالَّذِيْنَ اِذَا ذُكِّرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ لَمْ يَخِرُّوْا عَلَيْهَا صُمًّا وَّعُمْيَانًا‏(73)\nWAL LAZEENA EZAA ZUKKEROOA BE-AAYAATIL RABBEHIM LAM YAKHERROOA A’LAYHAA SUMMAN WWAU’UMYAANAN.\nThose who, when they are admonished with the Signs of their Lord, droop not down at them as if they were deaf or blind; \nوَالَّذِيْنَ يَقُوْلُوْنَ رَبَّنَا هَبْ لَنَا مِنْ اَزْوَاجِنَا وَذُرِّيّٰتِنَا قُرَّةَ اَعْيُنٍ وَّاجْعَلْنَا لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَ اِمَامًا‏(74)\nWAL LAZEENA YAQOOLOONA RABBANAA HAB LANAA MIN AAZWAAJENAA WAZURREETENAA QURRATA AAA’YUNIN WWAAJA’ALNAA LILMUTTAQEEN AEMAAMAN.\nAnd those who pray, “Our Lord! Grant unto us wives and offspring who will be the comfort of our eyes, and give us (the grace) to lead the righteous.” \nاُولٰٓئِكَ يُجْزَوْنَ الْغُرْفَةَ بِمَا صَبَرُوْا وَيُلَقَّوْنَ فِيْهَا تَحِيَّةً وَّسَلٰمًا ۙ‏(75)\nOOLAAA-EKA YUJZAWNA AL-GHURFATA BEMAA SABAROO WAYULAQQAWNA FEEHAA TAHEETAN WWASALAAMAN.\nThose are the ones who will be rewarded with the highest place in heaven, because of their patient constancy: therein shall they be met with salutations and peace, \nخٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا‌ ؕ حَسُنَتْ مُسْتَقَرًّا وَّمُقَامًا‏(76)\nKHAALEDEENA FEEHAA HASUNAT MUSTAQARRAN WWAMUQAAMAN.\nDwelling therein;- how beautiful an abode and place of rest! \nقُلْ مَا يَعْبَؤُا بِكُمْ رَبِّىْ لَوْلَا دُعَآؤُكُمْ‌ۚ فَقَدْ كَذَّبْتُمْ فَسَوْفَ يَكُوْنُ لِزَامًا‏(77)\nQUL MAA YAA’BAUA BEKUM RABBEE LAWLAA DUA’AAUKUM FAQAD KAZZABTUM FA-SAWFA LAHUL LEZAAMAN.\nSay (to the Rejecters): “My Lord is not uneasy because of you if ye call not on Him: But ye have indeed rejected (Him), and soon will come the inevitable (punishment)!” ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Furqan (The Criterion)\nThis Surah has 77 verses and it is ‘Makki’. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that a person who recites this Surah will be taken to Jannah without questioning, provided he believes in the Day of Judgement and the Raising of the Dead (from the graves).\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) said that Allah (s.w.t.) will never send His punishment upon any person who recites this Surah every night. The reciter of this Surah will also gain a highly status in the hereafter. The person who writes this Surah and keeps it in his possession will never be harmed by the vermin of this earth."
